Based on the screenshot, the “pencil” icon button is being rendered with the standard “md” text‐button padding rather than the much tighter, equal padding that icon‐only buttons should have. In our code, the `IconButton` wrapper never tells `Button` that it’s an icon‐only button, so `Button` defaults to text-button styles (and pads the right side too much).

To fix this, we need to pass `hasIconOnly` (and, for proper a11y, `iconDescription`) down into `Button`. That will give it the correct `btn--icon-only` class and shrink the padding to the proper icon‐only dimensions.

